Finding: {"title":"/delete-user has no tenant scoping — any flight-school admin can delete any user account platform-wide","severity":"CRITICAL","area":"Authorization / multi-tenant isolation","files":["src/server/routes/routes-auth.ts"],"detail":"POST /delete-user (routes-auth.ts:879-939) is guarded only by requireAdmin() (role check: admin OR super_admin). Unlike the sibling endpoint /update-user-metadata (line 1046, which explicitly calls resolveSameOrgAuthUser to confirm the target belongs to the caller's school before writing), /delete-user resolves the target purely from the caller-supplied email or userId and calls auth.api.removeUser({ body: { userId: resolvedUserId } }) with zero org/tenant check. A regular flight-school 'admin' (not super_admin) can supply any other school's user email, or even another school's admin, and delete that account.","impact":"A single compromised or malicious flight-school admin account can delete arbitrary users across every tenant on the platform, including other schools' admins. This is a cross-tenant destructive action with no audit gate beyond the requireAdmin() role check, directly contradicting PDD-005's multi-tenant isolation intent and the pattern this file itself establishes elsewhere (resolveSameOrgAuthUser).","recommendation":"Call resolveSameOrgAuthUser(c, authUser, resolvedUserId) before invoking auth.api.removeUser, mirroring /update-user-metadata, and return 403 when it returns null. Reserve cross-tenant deletes for requireSuperAdmin().","confidence":"high"}
confirmed=true only if the defect genuinely exists. If misread → verdict="false-positive". If real but wrong severity → set correctedSeverity. If real but underspecified → verdict="needs-detail" (kept). Return JSON per the schema.

